[Music]  hey this is david2 and in this video  i'll be walking through new launches for  monitoring and telemetry  stick around to learn about service  directory and network intelligence  first off is something i'm really  excited to share service directory  provides a managed runtime service  catalog  that allows all of a customer's services  to be accessed from a single pane of  class  across google cloud on-prem and hybrid  environments  with service directory you have the  ability to look up services  services can use service directory to  look at each other up by name  instead of needing to know  infrastructure level details like ip  addresses  service directory can be queried via  http grpc  and dns service directory also gives you  the ability  to catalog services developers can  annotate and search for custom  properties on their services  for example if i'm trying to make a  service gdpr compliant  i might also want to use this  information dynamically to have the  service  only be allowed to communicate with  other gdpr compliance services  now instead of having multiple google  cloud apis determining which service is  gdpr compliant  an admin can easily identify all the  services that are gdpr compliant  with the service directory api  to recap service directory provides a  single pane of glass that discovers  registers and catalogs your services for  easy management  the next topic for monitoring and  telemetry is the network intelligence  center  network intelligence center provides a  single console for managing google cloud  network visibility monitoring and  troubleshooting  there are currently four modules to the  network intelligence center  network topology connectivity test  performance dashboard and firewall  insights  today we'll cover network topology and  connectivity test  for starters network topology is a  visualization tool for viewing the  topology of your vpc networks  and the metrics that are associated with  your google cloud resources  network topology shows actual traffic  flows between various networking nodes  including google cloud workloads and  network services like  load balancers and external clients and  associated  performance metrics one thing i'm  particularly excited about  is the ability to view your  infrastructure changes  you can look at topology evolution and  its associated metrics for six weeks of  history  this interactive visualization of the  topology helps reduce the time  spent to monitor and troubleshoot  workflows  it also helps you optimize your  architecture for better performance  and or cost continuing on with the  network intelligence center  will now cover in addition to the  connectivity test  as a refresher connectivity test is a  configuration and route  analyzer that lets you diagnose  connectivity issues  in your vpc network due to  misconfiguration  or due to missing routes when analyzing  network configurations  connectivity test uses an abstract state  machine to model  how a vpc network should process packets  google cloud processes the packet in  several logical steps  with this launch connectivity tests can  take into account the newly launched  hierarchical firewall policy rules  in addition to the previous vpc firewall  rules  for context hierarchical firewall  policies provide you the ability to  create firewall rules  not only at the vpc but at the folder  and organizational level  the connectivity test starts by checking  the hierarchical firewall policy  if connectivity is blocked by a  hierarchical firewall policy rule  the trace includes the name of the  policy if the connectivity is blocked by  a vpc firewall rule  the trace lists the name of the relevant  ingress or egress firewall rule  so this concludes our updates on  monitoring and telemetry  make sure to check out the links below  to get additional details on these new  features  join us again next time to learn what's  new in networking  you

